{"id":"eea5f574-6961-4b81-a3bc-ffe26877f211","object":"chat.completion","created":1793333830,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Table 4 and the conclusion are now available. I'll record the outlook note and then read the initial report to prepare the merge.\n\nOutlook note content (written verbatim as the note): \"Outlook notes (pp.51-52). Table 4 (p.51) lists five research agenda topics with challenges: 'Training Data' (finetune with inference-time reasoning data, convergent/stable RL, VLA/multimodal speech), 'Hallucination' (self verification, mechanistic interpretability, open-ended/open-world models), 'Agent Behavior' (scalable simulation infrastructure and role playing, distill reasoning to small models, models of agent/human behavior and emergent behavior), 'Self reflection' (in-model self reflection and metareasoning, metacognition/personality, automated scientific discovery) and 'Safety' (responsibility/liability, privacy/fairness, wider application areas). So agenda_topics = training_data, hallucination, agent_behavior, self_reflection, safety. Conclusion (Sec.5.2, p.52): 'Robotic interaction and tool-use build on grounded retrieval augmentation, social interaction (such as theory of mind) builds on self reflection, and all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification.' So shared_foundations = reasoning, self_verification. Safety (p.51) calls for multi-layer safeguards, continual adversarial training and red-teaming, self-regulation, and benchmarks such as AgentHarm.\"\n\n```python\nr = write_note(title='outlook', content=\"Outlook notes (pp.51-52). Table 4 (p.51) lists five research agenda topics with challenges: 'Training Data' (finetune with inference-time reasoning data, convergent/stable RL, VLA/multimodal speech), 'Hallucination' (self verification, mechanistic interpretability, open-ended/open-world models), 'Agent Behavior' (scalable simulation infrastructure and role playing, distill r