netune with inference-time reasoning data, stable RL, VLA/multimodal), 'Hallucination' (self verification, mechanistic interpretability, open-world models), 'Agent Behavior' (scalable simulation, role playing, distilling reasoning to small models), 'Self reflection' (in-model self reflection and metareasoning, metacognition/personality, automated scientific discovery) and 'Safety' (responsibility/liability, privacy/fairness, wider applications). So agenda_topics = training_data, hallucination, agent_behavior, self_reflection, safety. Conclusion (Sec.5.2, p.52): 'Robotic interaction and tool-use build on grounded retrieval augmentation, social interaction (such as theory of mind) builds on self reflection, and all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification.' So shared_foundations = reasoning, self_verification. Safety discussion (p.51) calls for multi-layer safeguards, continual adversarial training, red-teaming, self-regulation, standard benchmarks such as AgentHarm.\"\n\nThat's about 1000 chars. Good.\n\nquote for agenda in report: I'll use the table region continuous text.\n\nLet me craft quote carefully from extracted text (page 51):\n\n\"Training Data       Finetune with inference time reasoning data\n                             Convergent/stable reinforcement learning\n                             VLA, Multimodal signals, such as speech\n         Hallucination       Use Self Verification\n                             Use Mechanistic Interpretability\n                             Use Open Ended/Open World Models for exploration\n         Agent Behavior      Scalable simulation infrastructure, role playing\n                             Distill reasoning to small models\n                             Models of agent and human behavior, emergent behavior, future of society\n         Self reflection     In-model self reflection and metareasoning\n                             Metacognition, personality\n                             Automated Scientific D